course: dictionary
lesson: 8038
title: Words for stand-in rulers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A regent is a person who rules a country for a king or queen who is too young, ill or away. The clues are in the word's job: they are standing in for someone who cannot rule.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Princess Olha ruled Kyiv as regent (ruling for her young son) after her husband Ihor was killed in 945.» The bracket tells you what regent means, and the words "young son" and "killed" explain why she was in charge.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: "Princess Olha ruled Kyiv as a stand-in for her young son." It still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: A regent rules for a king or queen who is too young, ill or away.
fact: In the US, a regent can also be a member of a board that runs a university or schools.
fact: The Regency was the time in Britain from 1811 to 1820, when the future George IV ruled as Prince Regent.
fact: Regent Street and Regent's Park in London are named after the Prince Regent.
fact: «Princess Olha» ruled Kyiv as regent, but the story of her burning a town with pigeons is a chronicle legend, not proven history.
exercise: «Princess Olha ruled Kyiv as regent after her husband Ihor was killed.» What is a regent? | *A person who rules for a king or queen who is too young, ill or away | A shop on a famous London street | A soldier who guards a castle wall | A king who has just been crowned
exercise: What does «act as regent» most likely mean? | To act in a play on stage | To be a famous actor | To speak in a loud voice | *To rule in place of a king or queen who cannot
exercise: Which London street is named after the Prince Regent? | Baker Street | *Regent Street | Oxford Street | Downing Street
test: In «Princess Olha ruled Kyiv as regent (ruling for her young son)», what is the bracket doing? | Showing the date | *Explaining what regent means | Giving a long quote | Naming the city
test: The Regency lasted from 1811 to 1820 in Britain. Who ruled during it? | Oliver Cromwell | *The future George IV, as Prince Regent | Lady Jane Grey | The young Queen Victoria
exam: In a story, a regent may try to steal the throne. What does this suggest about the regent? | The regent has just won a prize | The regent is a kind teacher | *The regent may be a villain who wants power | The regent is a horse
